      "title": "Understanding the API Request",
      "sourceHash": "313f2f53ef4a8632931daf817911cba648cdf6464b0cf41ce19a7ff29b79e96e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "When running our Python code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 8.7,
          "en": "we received this output down here in the terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 12.54,
          "en": "This output is the API response we received,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 15.69,
          "en": "and as we learned in this module, to get a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.69,
          "end": 18.39,
          "en": "we have to send a request first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.39,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "In this request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "we have to define what type of information, what question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 28.29,
          "en": "what prompt in the end we want to send to the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.29,
          "end": 31.77,
          "en": "Now, the whole management of this request, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.77,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "is defined inside our completion variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 38.643,
          "en": "specifically inside this \"create\" function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "This function contains different so-called parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "like model and messages in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "and these parameters configure the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "So, one of the parameters we have to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "to send the request is the model parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "We talked about this on the slide already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "In our case, we use the GPT 3.5 Turbo model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 64.92,
          "en": "We could also use GPT Four instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "for example, or other models,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.43,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "but keep in mind that depending on the endpoint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 74.49,
          "en": "chat completion, or completion, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.49,
          "end": 77.163,
          "en": "only specific models are supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "Besides the model parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "we also have this messages parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 86.37,
          "en": "Messages, so plural here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.37,
          "end": 89.19,
          "en": "We'll understand this in a few minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.19,
          "end": 90.023,
          "en": "For the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.023,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "we can't just analyze the messages parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 97.97999999999999,
          "en": "which contains a so-called list, a Python list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.97999999999999,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "and this list then contains a so-called dictionary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "Now, we won't dive too deep into Python",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 106.74000000000001,
          "en": "and programming in this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 108.36,
          "en": "but the idea of such lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.36,
          "end": 111.24000000000001,
          "en": "and such dictionaries is to store information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.24000000000001,
          "end": 113.643,
          "en": "which can then be accessed afterwards,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.09,
          "en": "and the list here allows us to store one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.09,
          "end": 121.23,
          "en": "single in this case, or multiple dictionaries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.23,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "so this part here in the Colibrasis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 126.27,
          "en": "is one single dictionary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.27,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "and the dictionary always contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "so-called key and value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 137.31,
          "en": "So, the key here is roll and the value is user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.31,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "For the second key value pair inside this dictionary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "we have content, and content here is just \"hello.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 148.92000000000002,
          "en": "Now, what this means in simple words is that we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.92000000000002,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "to send the following message to ChatGPT",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.563,
          "en": "when sending our request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 158.04,
          "en": "Our role is the role of the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.04,
          "end": 163.04,
          "en": "so we are the person that wants to interact with the API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "and the content, the second key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "we want to send to the API is simply \"hello.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "If we would change this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 174.933,
          "en": "from hello to a question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 181.79,
          "en": "like, for example, what is the capital of France?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.65,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "And now, rerun our Python file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "We get back, \"The capital of France is Paris.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "So therefore, with the user role in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 197.4,
          "en": "and the content key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.4,
          "end": 202.323,
          "en": "we can define what the user wants to ask the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 205.2,
          "en": "Now, to make this a bit more interactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "instead of hard-coding the user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "we can just add a dedicated variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "for this user input that allows the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "to directly ask the question or write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "down the instruction in the terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "For this, we'll just create a user input variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 226.5,
          "en": "and set it equal to input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "Input here is a Python function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 233.043,
          "en": "a predefined Python function, which could just say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.117,
          "end": 239.97,
          "en": "\"Add your prompt in here.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.97,
          "end": 242.13,
          "en": "Now, we add a space, and with this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 245.22,
          "en": "we can replace this hard-coded value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.22,
          "end": 248.553,
          "en": "for the content key with user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.51,
          "end": 254.51,
          "en": "By now, rerunning our code, we get \"Add your prompt,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 259.5,
          "en": "and now, we could ask, what is Python, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 259.5,
          "end": 263.64300000000003,
          "en": "and by hitting enter, we get back the answer from the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 266.22,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "So, this is how we send our request in a very simple form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 273.9,
          "en": "Before we have a closer look at the answer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.9,
          "end": 276.06,
          "en": "at the response we get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.06,
          "end": 279.27,
          "en": "I wanna explore a few more core parameters we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 279.27,
          "end": 281.343,
          "en": "can add to our request.",
          "zh": ""
        }
